        "answer": {
          "short": "If Bob arrives first, Mary must arrive by $x+45$, so $y-x\\le45$. If Mary arrives first, Bob must arrive by $y+30$, so $x-y\\le30$.",
          "worked": "If Bob arrives first, he leaves at $x+45$ minutes after 6:00PM. They meet provided $y\\le x+45$, giving $y-x\\le45$.\n\nIf Mary arrives first, she leaves at $y+30$ minutes after 6:00PM. They meet provided $x\\le y+30$, giving $x-y\\le30$.\n\nBoth inequalities describe the meeting region; the inequality for the person who arrives later is automatically satisfied.",
