            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q49-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t=120-60\\sqrt3\\approx16",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " minutes (nearest minute).",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q49-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The two nonmeeting triangles have combined area ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(120-t)^2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". Set the remaining area fraction equal to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac14",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "With equal waiting times, they meet when $|x-y|\\le t$. For $0\\le t\\le120$, each nonmeeting triangle has perpendicular sides $120-t$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{meet})&=1-\\frac{2\\left(\\frac12(120-t)^2\\right)}{120^2}\\\\P(\\text{meet})&=1-\\frac{(120-t)^2}{14400}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor a meeting probability of $\\frac14$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{(120-t)^2}{14400}&=\\frac34\\\\(120-t)^2&=10800\\\\120-t&=60\\sqrt3\\\\t&=120-60\\sqrt3\\\\t&\\approx16\\text{ minutes (nearest minute).}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe positive square root is used because $120-t\\ge0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 98
